IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg7-governing-provisions`
IMPORT `dg7-nonstock-mergers`
IMPORT `dg7-merger-effects`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-rights`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-procedure`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-proceeding`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter IX, ss 255 to 262 -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece dg7).
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online made by a converter script;
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here has been verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation under the General Corporation Law (an
-- incorporator, a director or officer, a stockholder including a minority stockholder), asking what the Law lets them do, what it
-- requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them. In this Subchapter that person is a
-- director or member of a nonstock corporation that is merging (ss 255 to 258), a director, officer or stockholder of a corporation
-- that has merged (ss 259 to 261), or a stockholder who may demand an appraisal of the fair value of the shares (s 262).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list the module declares -- one
-- for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records and lists that the
-- layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called;
-- no rule is restated here. A record field that the rule called never reads is given a fixed placeholder, with a comment saying
-- so. Where the text does not answer, the layer-1 rule answers NOTHING and so does the question (the type is MAYBE).
-- The Court of Chancery, the Register in Chancery and the Secretary of State have no seat: what each does is asked as what the
-- person is owed or exposed to. A judgment the Law leaves to the Court (fair value, equity of costs, good cause for different
-- interest) is an input answered by the Court, never guessed.
--
-- Hohfeld: where a question is about a claim, privilege, power or immunity the person holds, the facts about the other party (the
-- corporation, the surviving entity, the plaintiff, the Secretary of State) are inputs, and the paired question about the
-- person's own duty or liability is the one beside it ("What must I ...?", "Can the Court ...?", "Am I bound by ...?").
-- Dates are asked as dates; the periods are the Law's own (20 days, 10 days, 60, 120), counted in calendar days with the last day inside.

§ `Helpers: building the records and lists the layer-1 rules take (no law)`

-- A list of n identical constituent corporations.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      c IS A `dg7 Constituent corporation`
GIVETH A LIST OF `dg7 Constituent corporation`
`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` n c MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE c FOLLOWED BY (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` (n MINUS 1) c)

-- The kinds of constituent corporation the questions mention. Only the facts the rules read are given: nonstock or stock, and where formed.
`dg7 seat a nonstock corporation of this State` MEANS
    `dg7 Constituent corporation` WITH
        `kind of corporation` IS `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
        `where the corporation is formed` IS `this State`

`dg7 seat a stock corporation of this State` MEANS
    `dg7 Constituent corporation` WITH
        `kind of corporation` IS `a stock corporation`
        `where the corporation is formed` IS `this State`

`dg7 seat a foreign nonstock corporation` MEANS
    `dg7 Constituent corporation` WITH
        `kind of corporation` IS `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable`
        `where the corporation is formed` IS `another jurisdiction of the United States`

`dg7 seat a foreign stock corporation` MEANS
    `dg7 Constituent corporation` WITH
        `kind of corporation` IS `a stock corporation`
        `where the corporation is formed` IS `another jurisdiction of the United States`

-- A merger or a consolidation, from the one yes-or-no fact.
GIVEN consolidating IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` consolidating MEANS
    IF consolidating
    THEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation formed by the consolidation`
    ELSE `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`

-- The agreement, from the twelve statements a person can say it makes.
GIVEN terms IS A BOOLEAN
      mode IS A BOOLEAN
      amendments IS A BOOLEAN
      attachment IS A BOOLEAN
      converted IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A BOOLEAN
      notOutstanding IS A BOOLEAN
      consideration IS A BOOLEAN
      surrender IS A BOOLEAN
      cashInLieu IS A BOOLEAN
      consistent IS A BOOLEAN
      foreign IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation`
`dg7 seat an agreement that states` terms mode amendments attachment converted manner notOutstanding consideration surrender cashInLieu consistent foreign MEANS
    `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation` WITH
        `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation` IS terms
        `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect` IS mode
        `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS amendments
        `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement` IS attachment
        `some shares, memberships or membership interests are to be converted or cancelled` IS converted
        `states the manner of converting or cancelling them` IS manner
        `some shares, memberships or membership interests are not to remain outstanding` IS notOutstanding
        `states the cash, property, rights or securities the holders are to receive in exchange for them` IS consideration
        `states the surrender of any certificates evidencing the shares, memberships or membership interests` IS surrender
        `provides for the payment of cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement` IS cashInLieu
        `that provision is consistent with s 155` IS consistent
        `states the provisions or facts the laws of each foreign jurisdiction require in an agreement of merger or consolidation` IS foreign

§ `Merging or consolidating with a nonstock corporation: ss 255 to 258`

-- Situation: your nonstock corporation (or a stock or foreign corporation merging with one) is merging or consolidating.
-- The group asks what the Law lets the corporations do, what the agreement must say, how it is approved and noticed, and
-- what the member or director is owed.

§§ `Section 255: nonstock corporations of this State`

-- s 255(a). Two or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit, may merge into one of them or consolidate
-- into a new resulting nonstock corporation, by an agreement that complies with, and is approved in accordance with, the section.
@export May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255 (s 255(a))?
GIVEN `the number of corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many corporations are taking part in the merger or consolidation?
      `how many of them are Delaware nonstock corporations` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those corporations are nonstock corporations organized under Delaware law (whether or not they are organized for profit)?
      `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the surviving corporation is one of the corporations merging` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a merger: is the surviving corporation one of the corporations that are merging? (If it is a consolidation, answer no.)
      `the new corporation is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a consolidation: is the new resulting corporation a nonstock corporation? (If it is a merger, answer no.)
      `our agreement complies with section 255 and has been approved in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement of merger or consolidation comply with section 255 and has it been approved as that section requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our nonstock corporations merge or consolidate under section 255` IF
    `s 255(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the surviving corporation is one of the corporations merging` `the new corporation is a nonstock corporation` `our agreement complies with section 255 and has been approved in accordance with it`
    WHERE
        constituents MEANS
            append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `how many of them are Delaware nonstock corporations` `dg7 seat a nonstock corporation of this State`)
                   (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` (`the number of corporations taking part` MINUS `how many of them are Delaware nonstock corporations`) `dg7 seat a foreign stock corporation`)

-- s 255(b) items (1) to (6). The agreement must state the terms and conditions, the mode of carrying the merger into effect, for a merger the
-- amendments to (or a statement that nothing changes in) the survivor's certificate of incorporation, for a consolidation that the resulting
-- corporation's certificate is as attached, the manner of converting or cancelling memberships, and what holders of memberships that
-- do not remain outstanding are to receive; a cash-in-lieu provision must be consistent with s 155.
@export Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires (s 255(b))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `it states the terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how the merger or consolidation is to be carried into effect?
      `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a merger: does the agreement state the amendments to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, or say that the surviving corporation's certificate stays as it is?
      `it states that the new certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a consolidation: does the agreement state that the new corporation's certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment?
      `memberships are to be converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any memberships or membership interests to be converted into others, or cancelled?
      `it states how they are converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how they are to be converted or cancelled?
      `some memberships will not remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any memberships or membership interests not remain outstanding?
      `it states what those holders receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities that the holders of those memberships are to receive?
      `it provides for cash in place of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in place of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement for them?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that provision consistent with section 155 (fractions of shares)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our merger agreement state what section 255(b) requires` IF
    `s 255(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) ag
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the s 255(b) rule does not read the surrender-of-certificates statement or the foreign-law statement (those are ss 257(b) and 256(b)).
        ag MEANS `dg7 seat an agreement that states` `it states the terms and conditions` `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` `it states that the new certificate is attached` `memberships are to be converted or cancelled` `it states how they are converted or cancelled` `some memberships will not remain outstanding` `it states what those holders receive` FALSE `it provides for cash in place of fractions` `that provision is consistent with section 155` FALSE

-- s 255(b), last paragraph. The agreement is executed by an authorized person; if it is filed, it must be executed and acknowledged in
-- accordance with s 103.
@export Is our merger agreement properly executed (s 255(b))?
GIVEN `an authorized person executed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the agreement executed by an authorized person?
      `it is being filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement itself being filed with the Secretary of State (rather than a certificate of merger in its place)?
      `it was executed and acknowledged as section 103 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is filed: was it executed and acknowledged in accordance with section 103?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our merger agreement properly executed` IF
    `s 255(b) the agreement has been executed as the subsection requires` `an authorized person executed it` `it is being filed` `it was executed and acknowledged as section 103 requires`

-- s 255(b), ss 256(b), 257(b), s 261(a) (for a s 251 merger). A term may depend on facts outside the agreement if the manner in which they
-- operate is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement.
@export May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts outside the agreement (ss 255(b), 256(b), 257(b))?
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement itself clearly and expressly set out the manner in which those outside facts operate on the term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a term of our merger agreement depend on facts outside the agreement` IF
    `s 255(b) a term of the agreement may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate on the term`

-- ss 255(b), 256(b), 257(b), the sentence after the proviso. "Facts" includes, but is not limited to, an event, a determination or an action by a person
-- or body, the corporation included; whether anything else is a fact the sentence does not say (fork F-facts-1).
@export Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend (ss 255(b), 256(b), 257(b))?
GIVEN `what the term would depend on` IS A `dg7 Thing a term of the agreement may be made dependent upon` @desc What would the term depend on? Choose one of the options: an event occurring, a determination by a person or body (including the corporation), an action by a person or body (including the corporation), or something that is none of these.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a fact on which a term of our merger agreement may depend` IF
    `s 255(b) the thing is a fact in the sense of the sentence that defines facts` `what the term would depend on`

-- s 255(c). Notice of the meeting goes to each member who has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body and to
-- each other member entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws.
@export Must I, as a member, be given notice of the meeting on the merger (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `I have the right to vote for the election of the governing body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation?
      `I am entitled to vote on the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote on the merger under the corporation's certificate of incorporation or bylaws?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I, as a member, be given notice of the meeting on the merger` IF
    `s 255(c) the member is owed notice of the meeting` `I have the right to vote for the election of the governing body` `I am entitled to vote on the merger`

-- s 255(c). The notice must be given at least 20 days before the meeting.
@export By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given to me (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting of the members on the merger to be held?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must notice of the meeting on the merger be given to me` IS
    `s 255(c) the latest date for the notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting`

-- s 255(c). What the notice must say and how it must be sent.
@export Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `the date the notice was given to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting to be held?
      `it states the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the time of the meeting?
      `it states the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the place of the meeting?
      `it states the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the purpose of the meeting?
      `it contains a copy of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a copy of the merger agreement?
      `it contains a brief summary of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain a brief summary of the merger agreement?
      `it was sent to my address on the corporation's records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent to your address as it appears on the corporation's records?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the notice of the meeting I received good enough` IF
    `s 255(c) the notice satisfies the subsection` n
    WHERE
        n MEANS `s 255(c) Notice of the meeting` WITH
            `the date the notice was given` IS `the date the notice was given to me`
            `the date of the meeting` IS `the date of the meeting`
            `the notice states the time of the meeting` IS `it states the time`
            `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS `it states the place`
            `the notice states the purpose of the meeting` IS `it states the purpose`
            `the notice contains a copy of the agreement` IS `it contains a copy of the agreement`
            `the notice contains a brief summary of the agreement` IS `it contains a brief summary of the agreement`
            `the notice was sent to the member's address as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS `it was sent to my address on the corporation's records`

-- s 255(c). The agreement is adopted by a majority of the members entitled to vote (for the governing body, and any others entitled to vote
-- on the merger). Not covered where the counts cannot be a vote.
@export Have the members adopted the merger agreement (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `the number of members entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the corporation are entitled to vote (those entitled to vote for the governing body and any others entitled to vote on the merger)?
      `the number of those members who voted for adoption` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those members voted for adopting the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the members adopted the merger agreement` IS
    `s 255(c) the members of the corporation have adopted the agreement` `the number of members entitled to vote` `the number of those members who voted for adoption`

-- s 255(c) and (d). The adoption is certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary, unless a certificate of
-- merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of the agreement.
@export Has the adoption been certified on the agreement as it must be (ss 255(c), 255(d))?
GIVEN `the officer who performs the secretary's duties certified it on the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer who performs the duties of the secretary certify the adoption on the agreement?
      `a certificate of merger is being filed instead of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed in place of the agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the adoption been certified on the agreement as it must be` IF
    `s 255(c) the adoption has been certified as the subsection requires` `the officer who performs the secretary's duties certified it on the agreement` `a certificate of merger is being filed instead of the agreement`

-- s 255(d). Where no member has a vote except the members of the governing body themselves, a majority of all of the governing body suffices.
@export Can our governing body approve the merger on its own (s 255(d))?
GIVEN `no one but the governing body has a vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, is there no member with the right to vote for the governing body or on the merger other than the members of the governing body themselves?
      `the number of members of the governing body` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the governing body have in all?
      `the number of them who adopted the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the governing body adopted the resolution approving the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can our governing body approve the merger on its own` IS
    `s 255(d) the governing body alone has approved the agreement` `no one but the governing body has a vote` `the number of members of the governing body` `the number of them who adopted the resolution`

-- s 255(b), (c), (d) together: one constituent corporation's approval.
@export Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires (ss 255(b), 255(c), 255(d))?
GIVEN `our governing body adopted a resolution approving the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the governing body adopt a resolution approving the agreement?
      `no one but the governing body has a vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, is there no member with the right to vote for the governing body or on the merger other than the members of the governing body themselves?
      `the number of members of the governing body` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the governing body have in all?
      `the number of them who adopted the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members of the governing body adopted the resolution?
      `the number of members entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are entitled to vote on the agreement (0 if only the governing body votes)?
      `the number of those members who voted for adoption` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those members voted for adopting the agreement?
      `the officer who performs the secretary's duties certified it on the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the officer who performs the duties of the secretary certify the adoption on the agreement?
      `a certificate of merger is being filed instead of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed in place of the agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our corporation approved the merger agreement as section 255 requires` IS
    `s 255 the constituent corporation has approved the agreement` approval
    WHERE
        approval MEANS `dg7 s 255 Approval by one constituent corporation` WITH
            `the governing body adopted a resolution approving the agreement` IS `our governing body adopted a resolution approving the agreement`
            `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger` IS `no one but the governing body has a vote`
            `the number of members of the governing body` IS `the number of members of the governing body`
            `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution` IS `the number of them who adopted the resolution`
            `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement` IS `the number of members entitled to vote`
            `the number of those members who voted for adoption` IS `the number of those members who voted for adoption`
            `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary` IS `the officer who performs the secretary's duties certified it on the agreement`
            `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` IS `a certificate of merger is being filed instead of the agreement`

-- s 255(c). The merger becomes effective, in accordance with s 103, once each constituent corporation has adopted and certified the agreement.
@export When does our merger become effective (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `every constituent corporation has adopted and certified the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has each corporation that is a party adopted the agreement and certified its adoption (or filed a certificate of merger in place of the agreement)?
      `the date the filing becomes effective under section 103` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the filing of the agreement (or of the certificate of merger) become effective under section 103?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `When does our merger become effective` IS
    `s 255(c) the date on which the merger or consolidation becomes effective` (LIST `every constituent corporation has adopted and certified the agreement`) `the date the filing becomes effective under section 103`

-- s 255(c), last sentence. The last sentence of s 251(c) (a certificate of merger in place of the agreement, with a copy of the agreement
-- furnished free to any stockholder on request) applies, and "stockholder" includes "member".
@export Am I, as a member, treated as a stockholder for the certificate-of-merger provisions of section 251(c) (s 255(c))?
GIVEN `I am a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of one of the constituent corporations?
      `I am a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of one of the constituent nonstock corporations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a member, treated as a stockholder for the certificate-of-merger provisions of section 251(c)` IF
    `s 255(c) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of the last sentence of s 251(c)` `I am a stockholder` `I am a member`

-- ss 255(c), (e), (f). Which provisions of s 251 are brought in by section 255.
@export Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255 (ss 255(c), 255(e), 255(f))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference` @desc Which provision do you mean? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of section 251 apply to our merger under section 255` IF
    `s 255 the provision applies to a merger under this section` `the provision`

-- s 255(e). How the references in s 251(d) are read for a nonstock corporation.
@export How is this reference in section 251(d) read for our nonstock corporation (s 255(e))?
GIVEN `the reference` IS A `dg7 Reference in s 251(d)` @desc Which reference in section 251(d) do you mean? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A `dg7 Reference as read for a constituent nonstock corporation`
DECIDE `How is this reference in section 251(d) read for our nonstock corporation` IS
    `s 255(e) the reference in s 251(d) is read for a constituent nonstock corporation as` `the reference`

-- s 255(g). A charitable nonstock corporation cannot be merged into a nonstock corporation if its charitable status would be lost or impaired.
@export Does section 255 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status (s 255(g))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the other? Choose one of the options.
      `the corporation it is merged into` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one it is being merged into? Choose one of the options.
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merged corporation's charitable status be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 255 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` IF
    `s 255(g) this section does not authorize the merger` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the corporation being merged` `the corporation it is merged into` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

@export May a nonstock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives (s 255(g))?
GIVEN `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the charitable corporation? Choose one of the options.
      `the surviving corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the surviving corporation? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a nonstock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` IF
    `s 255(g) a nonstock corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation that continues as the surviving corporation` `the corporation being merged` `the surviving corporation`

§§ `Section 256: domestic and foreign nonstock corporations`

-- s 256(a). One or more Delaware nonstock corporations may merge or consolidate with one or more foreign nonstock corporations, unless the
-- law of the foreign jurisdiction prohibits it. The foreign law is not among the inputs: whether it prohibits the merger is a fact.
@export May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation (s 256(a))?
GIVEN `the number of Delaware nonstock corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are nonstock corporations organized under Delaware law?
      `the number of foreign nonstock corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are nonstock corporations organized under the law of another jurisdiction?
      `the number of other corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other corporations (for example, stock corporations) are taking part?
      `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the surviving corporation is one of the corporations merging` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a merger: is the surviving corporation one of the corporations that are merging? (If it is a consolidation, answer no.)
      `the new corporation is a nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of one of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a consolidation: is the new corporation a nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction in which one of the corporations is organized? (If it is a merger, answer no.)
      `the law of the foreign jurisdiction prohibits the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law of the jurisdiction under which a foreign nonstock corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation?
      `our agreement complies with section 256 and has been approved in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement comply with section 256 and has it been approved as that section requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our Delaware nonstock corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 256(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the surviving corporation is one of the corporations merging` `the new corporation is a nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of one of them` `the law of the foreign jurisdiction prohibits the merger` `our agreement complies with section 256 and has been approved in accordance with it`
    WHERE
        constituents MEANS
            append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of Delaware nonstock corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a nonstock corporation of this State`)
                   (append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of foreign nonstock corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a foreign nonstock corporation`)
                           (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of other corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a foreign stock corporation`))

-- s 256(a). Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation: a nonstock corporation organized under the law of any jurisdiction other than Delaware.
@export Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation (s 256(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation it is` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is it? Choose one of the options.
      `where it is organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is it organized? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this corporation a foreign nonstock corporation` IF
    `s 256(a) a foreign nonstock corporation` c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `dg7 Constituent corporation` WITH
            `kind of corporation` IS `the kind of corporation it is`
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where it is organized`

-- s 256(b). The agreement of all the constituent corporations states items (1) to (7); items (3) and (4) bite where the surviving or resulting
-- corporation is a corporation of this State; item (7) is whatever the laws of each foreign jurisdiction require.
@export Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires (s 256(b))?
GIVEN `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did all the constituent corporations enter into the agreement?
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting corporation a corporation of Delaware?
      `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `it states the terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how the merger or consolidation is to be carried into effect?
      `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a merger into a Delaware corporation: does the agreement state the amendments to its certificate of incorporation, or say that it stays as it is?
      `it states that the new certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a consolidation into a Delaware corporation: does the agreement state that the new corporation's certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment?
      `memberships are to be converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any memberships or membership interests to be converted into others, or cancelled?
      `it states how they are converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how they are to be converted or cancelled?
      `some memberships will not remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any memberships or membership interests not remain outstanding?
      `it states what those holders receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities that the holders of those memberships are to receive?
      `it provides for cash in place of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in place of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement for them?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that provision consistent with section 155 (fractions of shares)?
      `it states what the foreign laws require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the provisions or facts that the law of each foreign jurisdiction requires in an agreement of merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the merger agreement state what section 256(b) requires` IF
    `s 256(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) ag `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a Delaware corporation`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the s 256(b) rule does not read the surrender-of-certificates statement (that is s 257(b)).
        ag MEANS `dg7 seat an agreement that states` `it states the terms and conditions` `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` `it states that the new certificate is attached` `memberships are to be converted or cancelled` `it states how they are converted or cancelled` `some memberships will not remain outstanding` `it states what those holders receive` FALSE `it provides for cash in place of fractions` `that provision is consistent with section 155` `it states what the foreign laws require`

-- s 256(c). Each constituent corporation approves the agreement in accordance with the law under which it is organized, and a Delaware one in
-- the same manner as section 255 provides.
@export Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires (s 256(c))?
GIVEN `where the corporation is organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is this corporation organized? Choose one of the options.
      `it adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement as its own law requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it adopt, approve, certify, execute and acknowledge the agreement in accordance with the law under which it is organized?
      `if it is a Delaware corporation, it approved it in the manner of section 255` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a Delaware corporation: did it approve the agreement in the same manner as section 255 provides?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 256(c) requires` IF
    `s 256(c) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement as the subsection requires` a
    WHERE
        a MEANS `s 256(c) Approval by one constituent corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where the corporation is organized`
            `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged in accordance with the laws under which it is organized` IS `it adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement as its own law requires`
            `it is a Delaware corporation and was approved in the same manner as s 255 provides` IS `if it is a Delaware corporation, it approved it in the manner of section 255`

-- ss 256(c), (e), (f). Which provisions of ss 251 and 252 are brought in by section 256.
@export Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256 (ss 256(c), 256(e), 256(f))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference` @desc Which provision do you mean? Choose one of the options.
      `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation surviving the merger a corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 256` IF
    `s 256 the provision applies to a merger under this section` `the provision` ctx
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the s 256 rule reads only whether the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation.
        ctx MEANS `dg7 Context of a provision brought in` WITH
            `it is a merger and not a consolidation` IS TRUE
            `the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State` IS `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation`
            `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` IS FALSE
            `the constituent corporation concerned is a stock corporation of this State` IS FALSE

-- s 256(d). A surviving foreign nonstock corporation must agree that it may be served with process in this State, irrevocably appoint the
-- Secretary of State as its agent, and specify the address to which a copy of process is to be mailed.
@export Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `our surviving corporation is a foreign nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger a foreign nonstock corporation?
      `it agreed that it may be served with process in Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it agree that it may be served with process in Delaware in any proceeding to enforce an obligation of a constituent Delaware corporation or an obligation arising from the merger?
      `it irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process?
      `it specified the address for the copy of process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it specify the address to which a copy of process is to be mailed by the Secretary of State?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our surviving foreign nonstock corporation done what section 256(d) requires of it` IF
    `s 256(d) the surviving or resulting foreign nonstock corporation has done what the subsection requires of it` `our surviving corporation is a foreign nonstock corporation` `it agreed that it may be served with process in Delaware` `it irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent` `it specified the address for the copy of process`

-- s 256(d). Process may be served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission, but only as the Secretary of State prescribes.
@export Is my electronic service of process on the Secretary of State good (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `I served it by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the process on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission?
      `I did it as the Secretary of State prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do it in the way the Secretary of State has prescribed for electronic service?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my electronic service of process on the Secretary of State good` IF
    `s 256(d) the service of process on the Secretary of State is good` `I served it by electronic transmission` `I did it as the Secretary of State prescribes`

-- s 256(d). The plaintiff must serve process and papers in duplicate, notify the Secretary of State that service is made under the subsection,
-- and pay the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29).
@export Have I done what section 256(d) requires of a plaintiff serving through the Secretary of State (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `I served the process and papers in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the process and any other papers in duplicate?
      `I notified the Secretary of State that service was made under section 256(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Secretary of State that service was being made under section 256(d)?
      `I paid the fee under section 391(a)(29)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what section 256(d) requires of a plaintiff serving through the Secretary of State` IF
    `s 256(d) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires of the plaintiff` `I served the process and papers in duplicate` `I notified the Secretary of State that service was made under section 256(d)` `I paid the fee under section 391(a)(29)`

@export Will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `I paid the fee under section 391(a)(29)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you pay the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under section 391(a)(29)?
      `I prevail in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prevail in the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the fee I paid the Secretary of State be taxed as part of the costs` IF
    `s 256(d) the fee is taxed as a part of the costs in the proceeding` `I paid the fee under section 391(a)(29)` `I prevail in the proceeding`

-- s 256(d). The Secretary of State's letter to the surviving corporation goes to the address it specified, or the last address it designated in
-- writing for the purpose.
@export To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter to our corporation (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `the address our corporation specified` IS A STRING @desc What address did the corporation specify for the copy of process to be mailed to?
      `we designated a different address in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation since designated, in writing to the Secretary of State, a different address for this purpose?
      `the last address we designated` IS A STRING @desc If so, what is the last address it designated? (Leave blank if none.)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `To what address must the Secretary of State mail the letter to our corporation` IS
    `s 256(d) the address to which the Secretary of State's letter must be directed` `the address our corporation specified` designated
    WHERE
        designated MEANS
            IF `we designated a different address in writing`
            THEN JUST `the last address we designated`
            ELSE NOTHING

@export Was the Secretary of State's letter to our corporation sent as section 256(d) requires (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `the Secretary of State notified us forthwith by letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Secretary of State notify the corporation of the service forthwith, by letter?
      `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier?
      `there is a record of delivery signed by the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient?
      `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and papers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the letter enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served?
      `the letter went to the right address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter directed to the address specified (or the last address designated in writing)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the Secretary of State's letter to our corporation sent as section 256(d) requires` IF
    `s 256(d) the Secretary of State's letter to the corporation is as the subsection requires` `the Secretary of State notified us forthwith by letter` `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit` `there is a record of delivery signed by the recipient` `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and papers` `the letter went to the right address`

-- s 256(d). The Secretary of State need not keep the record of the service for more than 5 years from receipt.
@export Can the Secretary of State now discard the record of the service (s 256(d))?
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the Secretary of State receive the service of process?
      `today's date` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today (or the date you are asking about)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Secretary of State now discard the record of the service` IF
    `s 256(d) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of the service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service` `today's date`

-- s 256(g). A charitable nonstock corporation cannot be merged into a nonstock corporation if its charitable status would be lost or impaired.
@export Does section 256 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status (s 256(g))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the other? Choose one of the options.
      `the corporation it is merged into` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one it is being merged into? Choose one of the options.
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merged corporation's charitable status be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 256 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` IF
    `s 256(g) this section does not authorize the merger` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the corporation being merged` `the corporation it is merged into` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

§§ `Section 257: stock corporations with nonstock corporations of this State`

-- s 257(a). One or more Delaware nonstock corporations may merge or consolidate with one or more Delaware stock corporations.
@export May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257 (s 257(a))?
GIVEN `the number of Delaware nonstock corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are nonstock corporations organized under Delaware law?
      `the number of Delaware stock corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are stock corporations organized under Delaware law?
      `the number of other corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other corporations (for example, corporations of another jurisdiction) are taking part?
      `our agreement complies with section 257 and has been approved in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement comply with section 257 and has it been approved as that section requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our Delaware nonstock and stock corporations merge or consolidate under section 257` IF
    `s 257(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents `our agreement complies with section 257 and has been approved in accordance with it`
    WHERE
        constituents MEANS
            append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of Delaware nonstock corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a nonstock corporation of this State`)
                   (append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of Delaware stock corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a stock corporation of this State`)
                           (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of other corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a foreign stock corporation`))

-- s 257(a). The surviving constituent corporation or the resulting corporation may be organized for profit or not, and may be a stock or a nonstock corporation.
@export May the surviving or resulting corporation be of this kind (s 257(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation do you want the surviving or resulting corporation to be? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the surviving or resulting corporation be of this kind` IF
    `s 257(a) the surviving or resulting corporation may be of this kind` `the kind of corporation`

-- s 257(b). The board of directors of each stock corporation, and the governing body of each nonstock corporation, adopts the resolution.
@export Which body must adopt the resolution approving the agreement for my corporation (s 257(b))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A `s 257(b) Body that adopts the resolution`
DECIDE `Which body must adopt the resolution approving the agreement for my corporation` IS
    `s 257(b) the body that must adopt the resolution` `the kind of corporation`

-- s 257(b). The agreement states items (1) to (6); item (5) also states the surrender of any certificates evidencing the shares or memberships.
@export Does the merger agreement state what section 257(b) requires (s 257(b))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `it states the terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how the merger or consolidation is to be carried into effect?
      `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a merger: does the agreement state the amendments to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, or say that it stays as it is?
      `it states that the new certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a consolidation: does the agreement state that the new corporation's certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment?
      `shares or memberships are to be converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any shares, memberships or membership interests to be converted into others, or cancelled?
      `it states how they are converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how they are to be converted or cancelled?
      `some will not remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any shares, memberships or membership interests not remain outstanding?
      `it states what those holders receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities that those holders are to receive?
      `it states the surrender of certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the surrender of any certificates evidencing them?
      `it provides for cash in place of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in place of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement for them?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that provision consistent with section 155 (fractions of shares)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the merger agreement state what section 257(b) requires` IF
    `s 257(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) ag
    WHERE
        -- Placeholder: the s 257(b) rule does not read the foreign-law statement (that is ss 256(b) and 258(b)).
        ag MEANS `dg7 seat an agreement that states` `it states the terms and conditions` `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` `it states that the new certificate is attached` `shares or memberships are to be converted or cancelled` `it states how they are converted or cancelled` `some will not remain outstanding` `it states what those holders receive` `it states the surrender of certificates` `it provides for cash in place of fractions` `that provision is consistent with section 155` FALSE

-- s 257(c). A stock constituent corporation approves the agreement as section 251 provides; a nonstock one, as section 255 provides.
@export In the manner of which section must my corporation approve the merger agreement (s 257(c))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is yours? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A `s 257(c) Section whose manner of approval governs`
DECIDE `In the manner of which section must my corporation approve the merger agreement` IS
    `s 257(c) the section whose manner of approval governs the constituent corporation` `the kind of corporation`

-- ss 257(c), (d), (e). Which provisions of ss 251 and 252 are brought in by section 257.
@export Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 257 (ss 257(c), 257(d), 257(e))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference` @desc Which provision do you mean? Choose one of the options.
      `it is a merger and not a consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a merger into a surviving corporation (answer no if it is a consolidation)?
      `the corporation concerned is a Delaware stock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the constituent corporation you are asking about a stock corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 257` IF
    `s 257 the provision applies to a merger under this section` `the provision` ctx
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: the s 257 rule does not read where the survivor is organized.
        ctx MEANS `dg7 Context of a provision brought in` WITH
            `it is a merger and not a consolidation` IS `it is a merger and not a consolidation`
            `the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State` IS TRUE
            `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` IS FALSE
            `the constituent corporation concerned is a stock corporation of this State` IS `the corporation concerned is a Delaware stock corporation`

-- s 257(f). A charitable nonstock corporation cannot be merged into a stock corporation if its charitable status would be lost or impaired; a stock
-- corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation that survives.
@export Does section 257 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status (s 257(f))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the other? Choose one of the options.
      `the corporation it is merged into` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one it is being merged into? Choose one of the options.
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merged corporation's charitable status be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 257 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` IF
    `s 257(f) this section does not authorize the merger` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the corporation being merged` `the corporation it is merged into` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

@export May a stock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives (s 257(f))?
GIVEN `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the charitable corporation? Choose one of the options.
      `the surviving corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the surviving corporation? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a stock corporation be merged into our charitable nonstock corporation that survives` IF
    `s 257(f) a stock corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation that continues as the surviving corporation` `the corporation being merged` `the surviving corporation`

§§ `Section 258: domestic with foreign stock and nonstock corporations`

-- s 258(a). One or more Delaware corporations, stock or nonstock, may merge or consolidate with one or more foreign corporations (a foreign
-- corporation includes a nonstock corporation of another jurisdiction), unless the foreign law prohibits it.
@export May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation (s 258(a))?
GIVEN `the number of Delaware corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are organized under Delaware law (stock or nonstock)?
      `the number of foreign corporations taking part` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the corporations taking part are organized under the law of another jurisdiction (stock or nonstock)?
      `the law of the foreign jurisdiction prohibits the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law of the jurisdiction under which a foreign corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation?
      `our agreement complies with section 258 and has been approved in accordance with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement comply with section 258 and has it been approved as that section requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our Delaware corporation merge or consolidate with a foreign corporation` IF
    `s 258(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents `the law of the foreign jurisdiction prohibits the merger` `our agreement complies with section 258 and has been approved in accordance with it`
    WHERE
        constituents MEANS
            append (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of Delaware corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a stock corporation of this State`)
                   (`dg7 seat n corporations that are all` `the number of foreign corporations taking part` `dg7 seat a foreign stock corporation`)

-- s 258(a). The surviving or resulting corporation may be a domestic or foreign stock corporation or a domestic or foreign nonstock corporation.
@export May the surviving or resulting corporation of a merger with a foreign corporation be of this kind (s 258(a))?
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation do you want the surviving or resulting corporation to be? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the surviving or resulting corporation of a merger with a foreign corporation be of this kind` IF
    `s 258(a) the surviving or resulting corporation may be of this kind` `the kind of corporation`

-- s 258(b). The agreement is as section 257 provides, and also sets forth what the laws of each foreign jurisdiction require.
@export Does the merger agreement state what section 258(b) requires (s 258(b))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `it states the terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation?
      `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how the merger or consolidation is to be carried into effect?
      `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a merger: does the agreement state the amendments to the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation, or say that it stays as it is?
      `it states that the new certificate is attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a consolidation: does the agreement state that the new corporation's certificate of incorporation is as set forth in an attachment?
      `shares or memberships are to be converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any shares, memberships or membership interests to be converted into others, or cancelled?
      `it states how they are converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state how they are to be converted or cancelled?
      `some will not remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will any shares, memberships or membership interests not remain outstanding?
      `it states what those holders receive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the cash, property, rights or securities that those holders are to receive?
      `it states the surrender of certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the surrender of any certificates evidencing them?
      `it provides for cash in place of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide for cash in place of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement for them?
      `that provision is consistent with section 155` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that provision consistent with section 155 (fractions of shares)?
      `it states what the foreign laws require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement state the provisions or facts that the law of each foreign jurisdiction requires in an agreement of merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the merger agreement state what section 258(b) requires` IF
    `s 258(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) ag
    WHERE
        ag MEANS `dg7 seat an agreement that states` `it states the terms and conditions` `it states the mode of carrying it into effect` `it states the amendments or that the certificate stays as it is` `it states that the new certificate is attached` `shares or memberships are to be converted or cancelled` `it states how they are converted or cancelled` `some will not remain outstanding` `it states what those holders receive` `it states the surrender of certificates` `it provides for cash in place of fractions` `that provision is consistent with section 155` `it states what the foreign laws require`

-- s 258(b). A Delaware constituent is approved by the method and procedure of section 257; a foreign one by the law under which it is organized.
@export Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires (s 258(b))?
GIVEN `where the corporation is organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law is this corporation organized? Choose one of the options.
      `it adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement as its own law requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a foreign corporation: did it adopt, approve, certify, execute and acknowledge the agreement in accordance with the law under which it is organized?
      `if it is a Delaware corporation, it used the method and procedure of section 257` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a Delaware corporation: did it approve the agreement by the method and procedure that section 257 prescribes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has this constituent corporation approved the agreement as section 258(b) requires` IF
    `s 258(b) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement as the subsection requires` a
    WHERE
        a MEANS `s 258(b) Approval by one constituent corporation` WITH
            `where the corporation is formed` IS `where the corporation is organized`
            `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged in accordance with the laws under which it is organized` IS `it adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged the agreement as its own law requires`
            `the corporation was approved by the method and procedure that s 257 prescribes` IS `if it is a Delaware corporation, it used the method and procedure of section 257`

-- s 258(c). Where the survivor is a foreign corporation and a certificate of merger is filed, the appointment of the Secretary of State to
-- receive process is included in the certificate.
@export Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process (s 258(c))?
GIVEN `our surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger a foreign corporation?
      `a certificate of merger is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a certificate of merger or consolidation being filed?
      `the certificate includes the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the certificate of merger include the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process` IF
    `s 258(c) the appointment of the Secretary of State is included in the certificate of merger or consolidation as the subsection requires` `our surviving corporation is a foreign corporation` `a certificate of merger is filed` `the certificate includes the appointment`

-- ss 258(c). Which provisions of ss 251 and 252 are brought in by section 258.
@export Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258 (s 258(c))?
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference` @desc Which provision do you mean? Choose one of the options.
      `it is a merger and not a consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a merger into a surviving corporation (answer no if it is a consolidation)?
      `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation surviving the merger a corporation of Delaware?
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the surviving or resulting corporation a foreign corporation?
      `the corporation concerned is a Delaware stock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the constituent corporation you are asking about a stock corporation of Delaware?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this provision of section 251 or 252 apply to our merger under section 258` IF
    `s 258 the provision applies to a merger under this section` `the provision` ctx
    WHERE
        ctx MEANS `dg7 Context of a provision brought in` WITH
            `it is a merger and not a consolidation` IS `it is a merger and not a consolidation`
            `the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State` IS `the surviving corporation is a Delaware corporation`
            `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation` IS `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation`
            `the constituent corporation concerned is a stock corporation of this State` IS `the corporation concerned is a Delaware stock corporation`

-- s 258(d). A charitable nonstock corporation cannot be merged into a stock corporation if its charitable status would be lost or impaired.
@export Does section 258 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status (s 258(d))?
GIVEN `we are consolidating into a new corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a consolidation into a new corporation? Answer no if it is a merger into one of the corporations.
      `the corporation being merged` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one being merged into the other? Choose one of the options.
      `the corporation it is merged into` IS A `Kind of corporation` @desc What kind of corporation is the one it is being merged into? Choose one of the options.
      `its charitable status would be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the merged corporation's charitable status be lost or impaired by the merger?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 258 forbid our merger because a charitable nonstock corporation would lose its charitable status` IF
    `s 258(d) this section does not authorize the merger` (`dg7 seat a merger or a consolidation` `we are consolidating into a new corporation`) `the corporation being merged` `the corporation it is merged into` `its charitable status would be lost or impaired`

§ `After the merger: ss 259 to 261`

-- Situation: a merger or consolidation has become effective, or is being planned, and you ask what follows for the corporation, its
-- property, its debts and its pending actions; what the surviving corporation may issue; and what the agreement may provide.

§§ `Section 259: status, rights and liabilities after a merger or consolidation`

-- s 259(a). Once a merger or consolidation is effective under this chapter, the separate existence of the constituent corporations ceases
-- (except the one into which the others are merged), their rights, property and debts pass to and bind the survivor, title to real estate is
-- not impaired and creditors' rights and liens are preserved.
@export Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation (s 259(a))?
GIVEN `the effect` IS A `s 259(a) Effect of a merger or consolidation` @desc Which effect do you mean? Choose one of the options.
      `the merger or consolidation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the merger or consolidation become effective under the General Corporation Law (at the time fixed under section 103)?
      `my corporation is the one the others were merged into` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your corporation the one into which the other constituent corporations were merged (the surviving constituent corporation)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this effect of a merger or consolidation follow for my corporation` IF
    `s 259(a) the effect follows` `the effect` status
    WHERE
        status MEANS `s 259 Status of a merger or consolidation` WITH
            `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter` IS `the merger or consolidation has become effective`
            `the constituent corporation concerned is the one into which the others have been merged` IS `my corporation is the one the others were merged into`

-- s 259(b). In a merger of banks or trust companies, fiduciary appointments and interests vest automatically in the surviving corporation,
-- without any order of a court.
@export Do the fiduciary appointments of a merged bank or trust company vest in the surviving corporation without a court order (s 259(b))?
GIVEN `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a merger of banks or trust companies?
      `the merger has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the merger become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the fiduciary appointments of a merged bank or trust company vest in the surviving corporation without a court order` IF
    `s 259(b) the fiduciary appointments and interests vest automatically in the corporation resulting from or surviving the merger` `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` `the merger has become effective`

-- s 259(b). Any party in interest may apply to an appropriate court or tribunal for a determination whether the surviving corporation continues
-- in the same fiduciary capacity or a new fiduciary is appointed.
@export May I, as a party in interest, apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary (s 259(b))?
GIVEN `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this a merger of banks or trust companies?
      `I am a party in interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party in interest in the fiduciary relationship (for example, a beneficiary or co-fiduciary)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a party in interest, apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary` IF
    `s 259(b) the person has the right to apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary` `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` `I am a party in interest`

§§ `Section 260: powers of the surviving or resulting corporation`

-- s 260(a). The corporation surviving or resulting from the merger (or the converted or domesticated corporation) may issue bonds or other
-- obligations up to the amount that, with its capital stock, covers the payments it must make and the obligations it must assume.
@export How much may our surviving corporation issue in bonds or other obligations (s 260(a))?
GIVEN `the payments and obligations the transaction requires` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in dollars, of the payments the surviving corporation must make and the obligations it must assume to carry out the merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication?
      `our capital stock` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corporation's capital stock, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may our surviving corporation issue in bonds or other obligations` IS
    `s 260(a) the most the corporation may issue in bonds or other obligations` `the payments and obligations the transaction requires` `our capital stock`

@export May our surviving corporation issue bonds or other obligations in this amount (s 260(a))?
GIVEN `a merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication into a Delaware corporation is taking place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are two or more corporations being merged or consolidated, or is another entity being converted to, or a non-United States entity domesticated as, a corporation of Delaware?
      `the amount of bonds or other obligations` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of bonds or other obligations, in dollars, do you want to issue?
      `the payments and obligations the transaction requires` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total, in dollars, of the payments the surviving corporation must make and the obligations it must assume to carry out the transaction?
      `our capital stock` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the corporation's capital stock, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our surviving corporation issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` IF
    `s 260(a) the corporation may issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` `a merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication into a Delaware corporation is taking place` `the amount of bonds or other obligations` `the payments and obligations the transaction requires` `our capital stock`

-- s 260(b). To secure bonds and obligations issued under s 260(a), the corporation may mortgage its corporate franchise, rights, privileges and property.
@export May our surviving corporation mortgage its franchise and property to secure those bonds (s 260(b))?
GIVEN `the mortgage secures bonds or obligations issued under section 260(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mortgage to secure the payment of bonds or obligations issued under section 260(a)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our surviving corporation mortgage its franchise and property to secure those bonds` IF
    `s 260(b) the corporation may mortgage its corporate franchise, rights, privileges and property` `the mortgage secures bonds or obligations issued under section 260(a)`

-- s 260(c). To effect the merger on the terms of the agreement (or the conversion or domestication on the terms of an approved plan), the
-- corporation may issue shares and securities in exchange for the constituent's interests, or cancel shares, rights, securities or interests.
@export May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction (s 260(c))?
GIVEN `the action` IS A `s 260(c) Action the corporation takes to effect the transaction` @desc Which action do you mean? Choose one of the options.
      `it is to carry out a merger or consolidation on the agreement's terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action to carry out a merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement?
      `it is to carry out a conversion or domestication on an approved plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action to carry out a conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms of a plan approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity?
      `the shares are issued in exchange for the constituent's interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are issuing shares or securities: are they issued upon conversion of, or in exchange for, the shares, rights or securities of (or interests in) a constituent corporation, converting entity or domesticating entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our surviving corporation take this action to carry out the transaction` IF
    `s 260(c) the corporation may take the action` `the action` `it is to carry out a merger or consolidation on the agreement's terms` `it is to carry out a conversion or domestication on an approved plan` `the shares are issued in exchange for the constituent's interests`

§§ `Section 261: what the agreement may provide; pending actions`

-- s 261(a). The agreements of ss 251 (other than a s 251(g) merger), 252, 254 to 258, 263 and 264 may contain the provisions of the subsection;
-- a merger under s 251(g), s 253 or s 267, a conversion (s 266) and a transfer (s 390) may not (fork F-261-1: the other reading is recorded).
@export May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows (s 261(a))?
GIVEN `the provision under which our merger is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is your merger effected? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our merger agreement contain the provisions that section 261(a) allows` IF
    `s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` `the provision under which our merger is effected`

-- s 261(a)(1)(i). A party that fails to perform, comply or consummate before the merger is effective is subject to the penalties or consequences
-- the agreement sets forth, in addition to other remedies at law or in equity.
@export Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth (s 261(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the provision under which our merger is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is your merger effected? Choose one of the options.
      `the agreement sets forth penalties or consequences for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the merger agreement set forth penalties or consequences for the failure the other party committed?
      `it failed to perform an obligation due before the merger takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the other party fail to perform its obligations under the agreement, in each case required to be performed before the merger becomes effective?
      `it failed to comply with a term due before the merger takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it otherwise fail to comply with the terms and conditions of the agreement, in each case required to be complied with before the merger becomes effective?
      `it failed to consummate the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it otherwise fail to consummate, or to cause the consummation of, the merger or consolidation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the other party to our merger agreement subject to the penalties or consequences it sets forth` IF
    `s 261(a)(1) the party is subject to the penalties or consequences set forth in the agreement` (`s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` `the provision under which our merger is effected`) `the agreement sets forth penalties or consequences for the failure` `it failed to perform an obligation due before the merger takes effect` `it failed to comply with a term due before the merger takes effect` `it failed to consummate the merger`

@export May the penalties in our merger agreement include an amount based on our stockholders' lost premium (s 261(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the provision under which our merger is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is your merger effected? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the penalties in our merger agreement include an amount based on our stockholders' lost premium` IF
    `s 261(a)(1) the penalties or consequences may include an amount based on the loss of the premium or other economic entitlement of the stockholders` (`s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` `the provision under which our merger is effected`)

-- s 261(a)(1)(ii). A corporation entitled under the agreement to receive such a payment may enforce the other party's obligation to pay and keep
-- the payment.
@export May our corporation enforce the other party's payment obligation and keep what it pays (s 261(a)(1))?
GIVEN `the provision under which our merger is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is your merger effected? Choose one of the options.
      `the agreement entitles us to receive such a payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement entitle your corporation to receive from the other party an amount representing such a penalty or consequence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our corporation enforce the other party's payment obligation and keep what it pays` IF
    `s 261(a)(1) the corporation may enforce the other party's payment obligation and retain the payment received` (`s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` `the provision under which our merger is effected`) `the agreement entitles us to receive such a payment`

-- s 261(a)(2)(i), (ii). A stockholder representative named in the agreement binds the stockholders of a Delaware constituent corporation, irrevocably,
-- from the requisite vote adopting the agreement.
@export Am I, as a stockholder, bound by the stockholder representative named in the merger agreement (s 261(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the provision under which our merger is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is your merger effected? Choose one of the options.
      `the agreement appoints a representative of the stockholders with sole and exclusive authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the merger agreement appoint one or more persons as representative of the stockholders of a Delaware constituent corporation, with the sole and exclusive authority to act for them under the agreement?
      `the agreement makes the appointment irrevocable and binding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that the appointment is irrevocable and binding on all those stockholders from and after the adoption of the agreement by the requisite vote?
      `the stockholders have adopted the agreement by the requisite vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the stockholders adopted the agreement by the requisite vote?
      `I am a stockholder of a Delaware constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a stockholder of a Delaware constituent corporation (including one whose shares are cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I, as a stockholder, bound by the stockholder representative named in the merger agreement` IF
    `s 261(a)(2) the appointment of the stockholder representative binds the stockholder` (`s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` `the provision under which our merger is effected`) `the agreement appoints a representative of the stockholders with sole and exclusive authority` `the agreement makes the appointment irrevocable and binding` `the stockholders have adopted the agreement by the requisite vote` `I am a stockholder of a Delaware constituent corporation`

-- s 261(a)(2)(iii). The representative provision may not be amended after the merger is effective, or only with the consent of the persons the agreement
-- specifies. Before the merger is effective the paragraph says nothing: not covered.
@export May the stockholder representative provision be amended (s 261(a)(2))?
GIVEN `the merger has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the merger or consolidation become effective?
      `the agreement says it may not be amended after the merger is effective` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that the provision may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective?
      `the agreement says it may be amended only with specified consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement say that the provision may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons it specifies?
      `those persons have consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the persons the agreement specifies consented to or approved the amendment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the stockholder representative provision be amended` IS
    `s 261(a)(2) the provision may be amended` `the merger has become effective` `the agreement says it may not be amended after the merger is effective` `the agreement says it may be amended only with specified consent` `those persons have consented`

-- s 261(a). A provision of the agreement adopted under the subsection may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement, if the manner in which
-- they operate is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement.
@export May a provision of our merger agreement under section 261(a) depend on facts outside the agreement (s 261(a))?
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement clearly and expressly set out the manner in which those outside facts operate on the provision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a provision of our merger agreement under section 261(a) depend on facts outside the agreement` IF
    `s 261(a) a provision may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets out how those facts operate`

-- s 261(b). A pending action or proceeding by or against a corporation that is party to the merger is prosecuted as if the merger had not taken
-- place, or the surviving corporation may be substituted.
@export Is the action or proceeding I have pending prosecuted as if the merger had not taken place (s 261(b))?
GIVEN `my action or proceeding is pending by or against a corporation that is party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding pending by or against a corporation that is a party to the merger or consolidation?
      `the merger or consolidation has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the merger or consolidation taken place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the action or proceeding I have pending prosecuted as if the merger had not taken place` IF
    `s 261(b) the pending action or proceeding is prosecuted as if the merger or consolidation had not taken place` `my action or proceeding is pending by or against a corporation that is party to the merger` `the merger or consolidation has taken place`

@export May the surviving corporation be substituted in the action or proceeding I have pending (s 261(b))?
GIVEN `my action or proceeding is pending by or against a corporation that is party to the merger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding pending by or against a corporation that is a party to the merger or consolidation?
      `the merger or consolidation has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the merger or consolidation taken place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the surviving corporation be substituted in the action or proceeding I have pending` IF
    `s 261(b) the surviving or resulting corporation may be substituted in the pending action or proceeding` `my action or proceeding is pending by or against a corporation that is party to the merger` `the merger or consolidation has taken place`

§ `Appraisal rights: section 262`

-- Situation: a stockholder (or a beneficial owner) of a Delaware corporation faces a merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or
-- continuance and asks whether the Court of Chancery will appraise the fair value of the shares, what to do and by when, and what follows.
-- The other party of every relation here is the corporation or the surviving, resulting or converted entity (its duties to notify, to pay and to
-- file the list) or the Court of Chancery (whose findings are inputs).

§§ `Do I have appraisal rights? Subsections (a), (b) and (c)`

-- s 262(b), (c). Appraisal rights are available for the shares of a class or series in a listed transaction, unless the class was listed or held by more than
-- 2,000 holders of record (or is the survivor's, with no stockholder vote needed under s 251(f)), restored if the holders must accept anything but the
-- permitted consideration (stock of the survivor, listed or widely held stock of another corporation, cash for fractions); a s 253 or s 267 subsidiary
-- not wholly owned; or the certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights for the event.
@export Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares (ss 262(b), 262(c))?
GIVEN `the provision under which the transaction is effected` IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected` @desc Under which provision of the General Corporation Law is the merger, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance effected? Choose one of the options.
      `my shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares those of a converted or domesticated corporation?
      `the transaction is authorized under section 265 or section 388` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction authorized pursuant to and in accordance with section 265 or section 388?
      `my class was listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time tested (the record date for notice of the meeting, or for consent under section 228, or immediately before the agreement under section 251(h) was signed), was your class or series of stock, or depository receipts for it, listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the number of holders of record of my class` IS A NUMBER @desc At that time, how many holders of record did your class or series of stock, or depository receipts for it, have?
      `my shares are those of the surviving corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your shares those of the constituent corporation that survives the merger?
      `the merger needed no vote of the survivor's stockholders under section 251(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the merger not require, for its approval, the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as section 251(f) provides?
      `I must accept stock of the survivor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders required to accept shares of the surviving or resulting corporation (or of the converted entity or the entity resulting from a transfer, domestication or continuance), or depository receipts for them?
      `that issuer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that issuer a corporation?
      `I must accept stock of another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders required to accept shares of any other corporation, or depository receipts for them?
      `that other stock will be listed on a national securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, will those shares (or receipts) be listed on a national securities exchange at the effective date?
      `the number of holders of record of that other stock at the effective date` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many holders of record will those shares (or receipts) have at the effective date?
      `I must accept cash in place of fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders required to accept cash in place of fractional shares or fractional depository receipts?
      `those fractions are of the kinds just described` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the fractions fractions of the shares or receipts described in the last four questions (the survivor's stock, or listed or widely held stock of another corporation)?
      `I must accept anything else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holders required to accept anything else (cash, property, rights or other securities)?
      `the parent does not own all of the stock of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger under section 253 or section 267: does the parent not own all of the subsidiary's stock immediately before the merger?
      `our certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights for this event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation's certificate of incorporation provide that appraisal rights are available for this kind of event?
      `the event` IS A `s 262(c) Event for which the certificate may provide appraisal rights` @desc Which kind of event is it? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are appraisal rights available for my class or series of shares` IF
    `s 262 appraisal rights are available for the shares` t `the events the certificate provides` `the event`
    WHERE
        itemOfSurvivorStock MEANS `s 262(b)(2) Item of consideration` WITH
            `what the holders are required to accept` IS `shares of stock of the surviving or resulting corporation, or of the converted entity or the entity resulting from a transfer, domestication or continuance, or depository receipts in respect thereof`
            `the issuer is a corporation` IS `that issuer is a corporation`
            -- Placeholders: limb a. does not read these fields.
            `the shares or depository receipts were listed on a national securities exchange at the effective date` IS FALSE
            `the number of holders of record at the effective date` IS 0
            `the fractional shares or depository receipts are of a kind described in a. or b.` IS FALSE
        itemOfOtherStock MEANS `s 262(b)(2) Item of consideration` WITH
            `what the holders are required to accept` IS `shares of stock of any other corporation, or depository receipts in respect thereof`
            `the shares or depository receipts were listed on a national securities exchange at the effective date` IS `that other stock will be listed on a national securities exchange`
            `the number of holders of record at the effective date` IS `the number of holders of record of that other stock at the effective date`
            -- Placeholders: limb b. does not read these fields.
            `the issuer is a corporation` IS TRUE
            `the fractional shares or depository receipts are of a kind described in a. or b.` IS FALSE
        itemOfCash MEANS `s 262(b)(2) Item of consideration` WITH
            `what the holders are required to accept` IS `cash in lieu of fractional shares or fractional depository receipts`
            `the fractional shares or depository receipts are of a kind described in a. or b.` IS `those fractions are of the kinds just described`
            -- Placeholders: limb c. does not read these fields.
            `the issuer is a corporation` IS TRUE
            `the shares or depository receipts were listed on a national securities exchange at the effective date` IS FALSE
            `the number of holders of record at the effective date` IS 0
        itemOfAnythingElse MEANS `s 262(b)(2) Item of consideration` WITH
            `what the holders are required to accept` IS `anything else`
            -- Placeholders: nothing is read of "anything else".
            `the issuer is a corporation` IS FALSE
            `the shares or depository receipts were listed on a national securities exchange at the effective date` IS FALSE
            `the number of holders of record at the effective date` IS 0
            `the fractional shares or depository receipts are of a kind described in a. or b.` IS FALSE
        items MEANS
            append (IF `I must accept stock of the survivor` THEN LIST itemOfSurvivorStock ELSE EMPTY)
                   (append (IF `I must accept stock of another corporation` THEN LIST itemOfOtherStock ELSE EMPTY)
                           (append (IF `I must accept cash in place of fractions` THEN LIST itemOfCash ELSE EMPTY)
                                   (IF `I must accept anything else` THEN LIST itemOfAnythingElse ELSE EMPTY)))
        t MEANS `s 262(b) Class or series in a transaction` WITH
            `the provision under which the transaction is effected` IS `the provision under which the transaction is effected`
            `the shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation` IS `my shares are those of a converted or domesticated corporation`
            `the transaction is authorized pursuant to and in accordance with the provisions of s 265 or s 388` IS `the transaction is authorized under section 265 or section 388`
            `the stock or the depository receipts in respect of it were listed on a national securities exchange` IS `my class was listed on a national securities exchange`
            `the number of holders of record of the stock or the depository receipts` IS `the number of holders of record of my class`
            `the shares are those of the constituent corporation surviving the merger` IS `my shares are those of the surviving corporation`
            `the merger did not require for its approval the vote of the stockholders of the surviving corporation as provided in s 251(f)` IS `the merger needed no vote of the survivor's stockholders under section 251(f)`
            `what the holders are required to accept` IS items
            `the parent owns all of the stock of the subsidiary Delaware corporation immediately prior to the merger` IS NOT `the parent does not own all of the stock of the subsidiary`
        `the events the certificate provides` MEANS
            IF `our certificate of incorporation provides appraisal rights for this event` THEN LIST `the event` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 262(b)(1). The date at which the class or series is tested for the listing and the 2,000-holder limits depends on how the transaction was approved.
@export As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders (s 262(b)(1))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 262(b)(1) The time at which the class or series is tested`
DECIDE `As of what time is my class or series tested for listing and the number of holders` IS
    `s 262(b)(1) the time at which the class or series is tested` `how the transaction was approved`

-- s 262(a). The first sentence: a holder of record of stock of a Delaware corporation who held on the date of the demand and continuously through the
-- effective date, has complied with subsection (d), and neither voted in favor nor consented in writing under s 228, is entitled to an appraisal
-- by the Court of Chancery of the fair value of the shares, in the circumstances of subsections (b) and (c).
@export Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares (s 262(a))?
GIVEN `appraisal rights are available for my class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are appraisal rights available for your class or series of shares under section 262(b) or (c)? (See the previous question.)
      `the corporation was formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law was the corporation whose stock you hold formed? Choose one of the options.
      `I hold the stock as holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the holder of record of the stock?
      `I held the shares on the date I made my demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you hold the shares on the date you made your demand?
      `I held the shares continuously through the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you held the shares continuously through the effective date of the transaction?
      `I have otherwise complied with subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you otherwise complied with subsection (d) (notice and demand)?
      `I voted in favor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you vote in favor of the transaction?
      `I consented in writing under section 228` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent to the transaction in writing under section 228?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of my shares` IF
    `s 262(a) the stockholder is entitled to an appraisal of the fair value of the shares` c `appraisal rights are available for my class or series`
    WHERE
        c MEANS `s 262(a) Claimant` WITH
            `the stock is stock of a corporation formed` IS `the corporation was formed`
            `the claimant holds the stock as holder of record` IS `I hold the stock as holder of record`
            `held shares of stock on the date of the making of the demand` IS `I held the shares on the date I made my demand`
            `continuously held the shares through the effective date` IS `I held the shares continuously through the effective date`
            `has otherwise complied with subsection (d)` IS `I have otherwise complied with subsection (d)`
            `voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance` IS `I voted in favor`
            `consented to it in writing pursuant to s 228` IS `I consented in writing under section 228`

-- s 262(a), defined terms.
@export Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 262 (s 262(a))?
GIVEN `I am a holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder of record of the stock?
      `the holding is stock in a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the holding stock in a corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a stockholder for the purposes of section 262` IF
    `s 262(a) a stockholder` `I am a holder of record` `the holding is stock in a corporation`

@export Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262 (s 262(a))?
GIVEN `I am the beneficial owner of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the beneficial owner of the shares?
      `they are held in voting trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held in voting trust?
      `they are held by a nominee for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held by a nominee on your behalf?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a beneficial owner for the purposes of section 262` IF
    `s 262(a) a beneficial owner` `I am the beneficial owner of the shares` `they are held in voting trust` `they are held by a nominee for me`

@export Is this instrument a depository receipt for the purposes of section 262 (s 262(a))?
GIVEN `it was issued by a depository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository?
      `it represents an interest in 1 or more shares or fractions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it represent an interest in one or more shares, or fractions of shares?
      `the shares or fractions are solely of stock of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those shares or fractions solely of stock of a corporation?
      `that stock is deposited with the depository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that stock deposited with the depository?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this instrument a depository receipt for the purposes of section 262` IF
    `s 262(a) a depository receipt` i
    WHERE
        i MEANS `s 262(a) Instrument` WITH
            `it is a receipt or other instrument issued by a depository` IS `it was issued by a depository`
            `it represents an interest in 1 or more shares, or fractions thereof` IS `it represents an interest in 1 or more shares or fractions`
            `the shares or fractions are solely of stock of a corporation` IS `the shares or fractions are solely of stock of a corporation`
            `that stock is deposited with the depository` IS `that stock is deposited with the depository`

§§ `Perfecting my appraisal rights: subsection (d)`

-- s 262(d). Paragraph (1) governs a transaction submitted to a meeting of stockholders; paragraph (2) one approved by consent under s 228, or under
-- s 251(h), s 253 or s 267.
@export Does paragraph (1) of section 262(d) govern how I perfect my appraisal rights (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph (1) of section 262(d) govern how I perfect my appraisal rights` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) paragraph (1) governs the transaction` `how the transaction was approved`

@export Does paragraph (2) of section 262(d) govern how I perfect my appraisal rights (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph (2) of section 262(d) govern how I perfect my appraisal rights` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) paragraph (2) governs the transaction` `how the transaction was approved`

-- s 262(d)(1). The corporation must notify each stockholder, not less than 20 days before the meeting.
@export By what date must the corporation notify me of the meeting at which appraisal rights are available (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting of stockholders on the transaction to be held?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the corporation notify me of the meeting at which appraisal rights are available` IS
    `s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the corporation's notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting`

@export Was the corporation's notice of the meeting given to me in time (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the date I was given the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the corporation's notice of the meeting given to you?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting to be held?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the corporation's notice of the meeting given to me in time` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the corporation's notice was given in time` `the date I was given the notice` `the date of the meeting`

@export Must the corporation notify me that appraisal rights are available (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `I was a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting?
      `I am a member who received notice under section 255(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a nonstock constituent corporation who received notice in accordance with section 255(c)?
      `appraisal rights are available for my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are appraisal rights available for your shares under section 262(b) or (c)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation notify me that appraisal rights are available` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the corporation must notify the person of the availability of appraisal rights` `I was a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting` `I am a member who received notice under section 255(c)` `appraisal rights are available for my shares`

@export Does the notice I received contain what section 262(d)(1) requires (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `it says that appraisal rights are available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares?
      `it includes a copy of section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a copy of section 262?
      `it includes a copy of section 114` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a copy of section 114?
      `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice direct you to a publicly available electronic resource where section 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost?
      `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 114` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice direct you to a publicly available electronic resource where section 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost?
      `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the constituent corporations, or the converting corporation, a nonstock corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice I received contain what section 262(d)(1) requires` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the notice has the contents the paragraph requires` n `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation`
    WHERE
        -- Placeholders: paragraph (1) does not read the statements of approval and of the effective date (those are paragraph (2)).
        n MEANS `s 262(d) Notice of appraisal rights` WITH
            `states that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares` IS `it says that appraisal rights are available`
            `states that the transaction has been approved` IS FALSE
            `includes a copy of s 262` IS `it includes a copy of section 262`
            `includes a copy of s 114` IS `it includes a copy of section 114`
            `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 262`
            `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 114`
            `states the effective date of the transaction` IS FALSE

-- s 262(d)(1). My demand: a separate written demand delivered to the corporation before the vote; a proxy or a vote against is not a demand.
@export Is my demand for appraisal good (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `I delivered it before the vote was taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver your demand to the corporation before the taking of the vote?
      `how I delivered it` IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered` @desc How did you deliver it? Choose one of the options.
      `it says who I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand reasonably inform the corporation of your identity?
      `it says I demand appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand reasonably inform the corporation that you intend to demand the appraisal of your shares?
      `it was a separate written demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a separate written demand (not merely a proxy or a vote against the transaction)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my demand for appraisal good` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the stockholder's demand is good` d
    WHERE
        d MEANS `s 262(d)(1) Demand before the vote` WITH
            `delivered to the corporation before the taking of the vote` IS `I delivered it before the vote was taken`
            `how the demand was delivered` IS `how I delivered it`
            `the demand reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder` IS `it says who I am`
            `the demand reasonably informs the corporation that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the stockholder's shares` IS `it says I demand appraisal`
            `the demand is a separate written demand and not merely a proxy or a vote against the transaction` IS `it was a separate written demand`

-- s 262(d)(1). Within 10 days after the effective date the surviving entity must notify each stockholder who complied and did not vote for or consent
-- to the transaction, and each beneficial owner who demanded, of the date it became effective.
@export By what date must the surviving entity tell me the date the transaction became effective (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the surviving entity tell me the date the transaction became effective` IS
    `s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the notice of the effective date` `the effective date`

@export Was the notice of the effective date given to me in time (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `the date I was told` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the surviving entity tell you the date the transaction became effective?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice of the effective date given to me in time` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the notice of the effective date was given in time` `the date I was told` `the effective date`

@export Must the surviving entity notify me of the date the transaction became effective (s 262(d)(1))?
GIVEN `I complied with subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with subsection (d)?
      `I voted in favor or consented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you vote in favor of the transaction or consent to it?
      `I am a beneficial owner who demanded appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the surviving entity notify me of the date the transaction became effective` IF
    `s 262(d)(1) the entity must notify the person of the date the transaction became effective` `I complied with subsection (d)` `I voted in favor or consented` `I am a beneficial owner who demanded appraisal`

-- s 262(d)(2). Where the transaction was approved by consent under s 228, or under s 251(h), s 253 or s 267: who gives the first notice and when.
@export Was the first notice of appraisal rights given to me in time (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `who gave the notice` IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who gives the notice` @desc Who gave you the first notice? Choose one of the options.
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the first notice of appraisal rights given to me in time` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) the first notice was given in time` `who gave the notice` `the date the notice was given` `the effective date`

@export Must the notice I received also state the effective date (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the notice I received also state the effective date` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) the notice must also state the effective date` `the date the notice was given` `the effective date`

@export Does the notice I received contain what section 262(d)(2) requires (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `it says the transaction was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say that the transaction has been approved?
      `it says that appraisal rights are available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice say that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares?
      `it includes a copy of section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a copy of section 262?
      `it includes a copy of section 114` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice include a copy of section 114?
      `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice direct you to a publicly available electronic resource where section 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost?
      `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 114` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice direct you to a publicly available electronic resource where section 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost?
      `it states the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the effective date of the transaction?
      `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is one of the constituent corporations, or the converting corporation, a nonstock corporation?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice I received contain what section 262(d)(2) requires` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) the notice has the contents the paragraph requires` n `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` `the date the notice was given` `the effective date`
    WHERE
        n MEANS `s 262(d) Notice of appraisal rights` WITH
            `states that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares` IS `it says that appraisal rights are available`
            `states that the transaction has been approved` IS `it says the transaction was approved`
            `includes a copy of s 262` IS `it includes a copy of section 262`
            `includes a copy of s 114` IS `it includes a copy of section 114`
            `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 262`
            `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS `it directs me to a free electronic copy of section 114`
            `states the effective date of the transaction` IS `it states the effective date`

-- s 262(d)(2). My demand must be made within 20 days after the notice is given (for a s 251(h) merger, within the later of the consummation of the
-- offer and 20 days after the notice).
@export By what date must I demand appraisal after the notice (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger under section 251(h): has the offer been consummated?
      `the date the offer was consummated` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was the offer consummated?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what date must I demand appraisal after the notice` IS
    `s 262(d)(2) the last day for the stockholder's demand` `how the transaction was approved` `the date the notice was given` consummation
    WHERE
        consummation MEANS
            IF `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated`
            THEN JUST `the date the offer was consummated`
            ELSE NOTHING

@export Is my demand for appraisal good after the notice (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given to you?
      `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger under section 251(h): has the offer been consummated?
      `the date the offer was consummated` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was the offer consummated?
      `the date I delivered my demand` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deliver your demand to the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
      `how I delivered it` IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered` @desc How did you deliver it? Choose one of the options.
      `it says who I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand reasonably inform the entity of your identity?
      `it says I demand appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand reasonably inform the entity that you intend to demand the appraisal of your shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my demand for appraisal good after the notice` IS
    `s 262(d)(2) the stockholder's demand is good` d (`s 262(d)(2) the last day for the stockholder's demand` `how the transaction was approved` `the date the notice was given` consummation)
    WHERE
        consummation MEANS
            IF `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated`
            THEN JUST `the date the offer was consummated`
            ELSE NOTHING
        d MEANS `s 262(d)(2) Demand after the notice` WITH
            `the date the demand was delivered` IS `the date I delivered my demand`
            `how the demand was delivered` IS `how I delivered it`
            `the demand reasonably informs the entity of the identity of the stockholder` IS `it says who I am`
            `the demand reasonably informs the entity that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the holder's shares` IS `it says I demand appraisal`

-- s 262(d)(2). A second notice of the effective date, where the first did not give it.
@export Must I be sent a second notice of the effective date (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `the first notice stated the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the first notice state the effective date of the transaction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be sent a second notice of the effective date` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) a second notice is required` `the first notice stated the effective date`

@export Was the second notice sent to me in time (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `who sent the second notice` IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who gives the notice` @desc Who sent you the second notice? Choose one of the options.
      `the date the second notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the second notice sent?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the second notice sent to me in time` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) the second notice was sent in time` `who sent the second notice` `the date the second notice was sent` `the effective date`

@export Must the second notice be sent to me (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `how the transaction was approved` IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved` @desc How was the transaction approved? Choose one of the options.
      `the date the first notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first notice sent?
      `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In a merger under section 251(h): has the offer been consummated?
      `the date the offer was consummated` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was the offer consummated?
      `the date the second notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the second notice sent?
      `I am entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a holder entitled to appraisal rights?
      `I demanded appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you demand appraisal under paragraph (d)(2), or (as a beneficial owner) under paragraph (d)(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the second notice be sent to me` IS
    `s 262(d)(2) the second notice must be sent to the holder` `the date the second notice was sent` lastDay `I am entitled to appraisal rights` `I demanded appraisal`
    WHERE
        consummation MEANS
            IF `the offer under section 251(h) has been consummated`
            THEN JUST `the date the offer was consummated`
            ELSE NOTHING
        lastDay MEANS `s 262(d)(2) the last day on which the second notice must go to every holder entitled to appraisal rights` `how the transaction was approved` `the date the first notice was sent` consummation

-- s 262(d)(2). An affidavit of the secretary, assistant secretary or transfer agent that the notice was given is prima facie evidence, absent fraud.
@export Is the affidavit that the notice was given prima facie evidence against me (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `who made the affidavit` IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who made the affidavit` @desc Who made the affidavit? Choose one of the options.
      `that person's corporation or entity is required to give the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation or entity of the person who made the affidavit required to give the notice?
      `it says the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit say that the notice has been given?
      `there was fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there fraud?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the affidavit that the notice was given prima facie evidence against me` IF
    `s 262(d)(2) the affidavit is prima facie evidence that the notice was given` `who made the affidavit` `that person's corporation or entity is required to give the notice` `it says the notice was given` `there was fraud`

-- s 262(d)(2). The record date for determining who gets the notice.
@export What is the record date for determining who is entitled to the notice (s 262(d)(2))?
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
      `the corporation fixed a record date in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fix a record date in advance?
      `the record date it fixed` IS A DATE @desc If so, what record date did it fix?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date for determining who is entitled to the notice` IS
    `s 262(d)(2) the record date for the notice` `the date the notice was given` `the effective date` fixed
    WHERE
        fixed MEANS
            IF `the corporation fixed a record date in advance`
            THEN JUST `the record date it fixed`
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 262(d)(3). A beneficial owner may demand in the beneficial owner's own name, on conditions.
@export Is my demand as a beneficial owner good (s 262(d)(3))?
GIVEN `I am a beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a beneficial owner (the owner of shares held in voting trust or by a nominee for you)?
      `the corporation was formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law was the corporation whose stock you own formed? Choose one of the options.
      `I held the shares on the date I made my demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you own the shares on the date you made your demand?
      `I owned the shares continuously through the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you owned the shares continuously through the effective date?
      `I have otherwise complied with subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you otherwise complied with subsection (d)?
      `I voted in favor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you vote in favor of the transaction?
      `I consented in writing under section 228` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consent to the transaction in writing under section 228?
      `my demand was made in writing in my own name as paragraph (1) or (2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your demand made in writing in your own name, in accordance with paragraph (d)(1) or (2), as applicable?
      `it identifies the holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your demand reasonably identify the holder of record of the shares?
      `it came with documentary evidence of my ownership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your demand accompanied by documentary evidence of your beneficial ownership of the stock?
      `it came with a statement that the evidence is a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it accompanied by a statement that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be?
      `it gives an address for notices and for the verified list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide an address at which you consent to receive notices and to be set forth on the verified list?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my demand as a beneficial owner good` IF
    `s 262(d)(3) the beneficial owner's demand is good` `I am a beneficial owner` c d
    WHERE
        c MEANS `s 262(a) Claimant` WITH
            `the stock is stock of a corporation formed` IS `the corporation was formed`
            -- Placeholder: a beneficial owner is not asked to be a holder of record; the rule that reads this claimant leaves that limb out.
            `the claimant holds the stock as holder of record` IS FALSE
            `held shares of stock on the date of the making of the demand` IS `I held the shares on the date I made my demand`
            `continuously held the shares through the effective date` IS `I owned the shares continuously through the effective date`
            `has otherwise complied with subsection (d)` IS `I have otherwise complied with subsection (d)`
            `voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance` IS `I voted in favor`
            `consented to it in writing pursuant to s 228` IS `I consented in writing under section 228`
        d MEANS `s 262(d)(3) The beneficial owner's demand` WITH
            `the demand is made in writing in the beneficial owner's name in accordance with paragraph (d)(1) or (2), as applicable` IS `my demand was made in writing in my own name as paragraph (1) or (2) requires`
            `the demand reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made` IS `it identifies the holder of record`
            `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of the beneficial owner's beneficial ownership of stock` IS `it came with documentary evidence of my ownership`
            `the demand is accompanied by a statement that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be` IS `it came with a statement that the evidence is a true copy`
            `the demand provides an address at which the beneficial owner consents to receive notices and to be set forth on the verified list` IS `it gives an address for notices and for the verified list`

§§ `The petition, withdrawal and statement of numbers: subsection (e)`

-- s 262(e). A petition may be filed within 120 days after the effective date by the surviving entity or by any person who has complied with subsections
-- (a) and (d) and is otherwise entitled.
@export By what date can a petition for appraisal be filed (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date can a petition for appraisal be filed` IS
    `s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date`

@export May I file a petition for appraisal (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `I am the surviving entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
      `I have complied with subsections (a) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with subsections (a) and (d)?
      `I am otherwise entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you otherwise entitled to appraisal rights?
      `the date I would file the petition` IS A DATE @desc On what date would you file the petition?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I file a petition for appraisal` IF
    `s 262(e) the person may commence an appraisal proceeding by this petition` `I am the surviving entity` `I have complied with subsections (a) and (d)` `I am otherwise entitled to appraisal rights` `the date I would file the petition` `the effective date`

-- s 262(e). Within 60 days after the effective date a person entitled to appraisal rights who has not commenced or joined the proceeding may withdraw the demand
-- and accept the terms offered upon the transaction.
@export May I withdraw my demand and accept the terms offered in the transaction (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to appraisal rights?
      `I have commenced the proceeding or joined it as a named party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party?
      `the date I would withdraw` IS A DATE @desc On what date would you withdraw your demand?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I withdraw my demand and accept the terms offered in the transaction` IF
    `s 262(e) the person may withdraw the demand and accept the terms offered` `I am entitled to appraisal rights` `I have commenced the proceeding or joined it as a named party` `the date I would withdraw` `the effective date`

-- s 262(e). A person who has complied with subsections (a) and (d), asking in writing within 120 days, is entitled to a statement of numbers from the surviving entity,
-- due within 10 days after the request or after the demand period ends, whichever is later.
@export Am I entitled to receive from the surviving entity a statement of the numbers of shares and holders (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `I have complied with subsections (a) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with the requirements of subsections (a) and (d)?
      `how I asked` IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered` @desc How did you make the request? Choose one of the options.
      `the date I asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to receive from the surviving entity a statement of the numbers of shares and holders` IF
    `s 262(e) the person is entitled to receive the statement` `I have complied with subsections (a) and (d)` `how I asked` `the date I asked` `the effective date`

@export By what date must the surviving entity give me the statement (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `the date the entity received my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the surviving entity receive your request?
      `the date the period for demands expired` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for delivery of demands for appraisal under subsection (d) expire?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the surviving entity give me the statement` IS
    `s 262(e) the last day for the statement` `the date the entity received my request` `the date the period for demands expired`

@export Was the statement given to me in time (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `the date I received the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the statement given to you?
      `the date the entity received my request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the surviving entity receive your request?
      `the date the period for demands expired` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period for delivery of demands for appraisal under subsection (d) expire?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the statement given to me in time` IF
    `s 262(e) the statement was given in time` `the date I received the statement` `the date the entity received my request` `the date the period for demands expired`

@export How many shares must the statement set out for a merger under section 251(h) (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `shares that were the subject of the offer` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares were the subject of the offer?
      `of those, excluded stock` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those shares, how many were excluded stock?
      `of those, tendered and accepted` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those shares, how many were tendered into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many shares must the statement set out for a merger under section 251(h)` IS
    `s 262(e) the number of shares the statement sets out for a s 251(h) merger` `shares that were the subject of the offer` `of those, excluded stock` `of those, tendered and accepted`

@export How many stockholders or beneficial owners must the statement count (s 262(e))?
GIVEN `record holders who demanded appraisal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many record holders demanded appraisal?
      `of those, record holders whose shares a beneficial owner demanded for` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those, for how many did a beneficial owner demand under paragraph (d)(3) for the same shares?
      `beneficial owners who demanded appraisal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many beneficial owners demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many stockholders or beneficial owners must the statement count` IS
    `s 262(e) the aggregate number of stockholders or beneficial owners the statement sets out` `record holders who demanded appraisal` `of those, record holders whose shares a beneficial owner demanded for` `beneficial owners who demanded appraisal`

§§ `The verified list: subsection (f)`

-- s 262(f). When a person other than the surviving entity files the petition, the entity has 20 days after service to file a duly verified list of the persons who
-- demanded and with whom no agreement as to value has been reached; an entity that petitions files the list with its petition.
@export By what date must the surviving entity file the verified list after my petition is served (s 262(f))?
GIVEN `the date my petition was served on the entity` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a copy of your petition served on the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what date must the surviving entity file the verified list after my petition is served` IS
    `s 262(f) the last day for the entity to file the verified list` `the date my petition was served on the entity`

@export Was the verified list filed in time (s 262(f))?
GIVEN `the date the list was filed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the verified list filed?
      `the date my petition was served on the entity` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a copy of the petition served on the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the verified list filed in time` IF
    `s 262(f) the verified list was filed in time` `the date the list was filed` `the date my petition was served on the entity`

@export Does the petition the surviving entity filed have the verified list it must have (s 262(f))?
GIVEN `the petition came with a duly verified list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the surviving entity's petition accompanied by a duly verified list?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the petition the surviving entity filed have the verified list it must have` IF
    `s 262(f) the petition filed by the entity has the list it must have` `the petition came with a duly verified list`

@export Must my name and address be on the verified list (s 262(f))?
GIVEN `I demanded appraisal for my shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you demand appraisal for your shares?
      `we have agreed a value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you and the surviving entity reached an agreement as to the value of your shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my name and address be on the verified list` IF
    `s 262(f) the person's name and address belong on the verified list` `I demanded appraisal for my shares` `we have agreed a value`

@export Must I be sent notice of the hearing by registered or certified mail (s 262(f))?
GIVEN `my name is on the list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your name shown on the verified list?
      `the Court ordered the Register to give notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered the Register in Chancery to give notice of the time and place of the hearing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be sent notice of the hearing by registered or certified mail` IF
    `s 262(f) the person must be sent notice of the hearing by registered or certified mail at the address on the list` `my name is on the list` `the Court ordered the Register to give notice`

@export Do I have to bear the costs of the notices of the hearing (s 262(f))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have to bear the costs of the notices of the hearing` IF
    `s 262(f) the party that bears the costs of the notices` EQUALS `a stockholder`

§§ `The hearing, the value and the payment: subsections (g) to (l)`

-- s 262(g). The Court may require a demanding holder of certificated stock to submit the certificates for notation, and may dismiss the proceedings as to one who fails to.
@export May the Court dismiss the proceedings as to me for not submitting my stock certificates (s 262(g))?
GIVEN `I demanded an appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you demand an appraisal for your shares?
      `my stock is represented by certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your stock represented by certificates?
      `the Court directed me to submit them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed you to submit your certificates of stock to the Register in Chancery for notation?
      `I have not complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to comply with that direction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Court dismiss the proceedings as to me for not submitting my stock certificates` IF
    `s 262(g) the Court may dismiss the proceedings as to the person for not submitting certificates` `I demanded an appraisal` `my stock is represented by certificates` `the Court directed me to submit them` `I have not complied`

-- s 262(g). If the shares were listed immediately before the transaction, the Court must dismiss the proceedings as to all holders unless more than 1% of the outstanding shares of the
-- class or series are for appraisal, or the consideration for them exceeds $1 million, or the merger was approved under s 253 or s 267.
@export Must the Court dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of my listed shares (s 262(g))?
GIVEN `the shares were listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the transaction, were the shares of your class or series listed on a national securities exchange?
      `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total number of shares entitled to appraisal?
      `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal are outstanding?
      `the value of the consideration for those shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in dollars, of the consideration provided in the transaction for that total number of shares?
      `the merger was approved under section 253 or section 267` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the merger approved pursuant to section 253 or section 267?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Court dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of my listed shares` IS
    `s 262(g) the Court must dismiss the proceedings as to all holders of the shares` s
    WHERE
        s MEANS `s 262(g) Shares seeking appraisal` WITH
            `the shares were listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the transaction` IS `the shares were listed on a national securities exchange immediately before the transaction`
            `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal` IS `the total number of shares entitled to appraisal`
            `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series eligible for appraisal` IS `the number of outstanding shares of the class or series`
            `the value of the consideration provided in the transaction for such total number of shares` IS `the value of the consideration for those shares`
            `the merger was approved pursuant to s 253 or s 267` IS `the merger was approved under section 253 or section 267`

-- s 262(h). The Court determines the fair value of the shares exclusive of any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction.
@export What is the fair value of my shares, leaving out the effect of the transaction (s 262(h))?
GIVEN `the Court's value of the shares including the effect of the transaction` IS A NUMBER @desc What value, in dollars, did the Court find for the shares including any element of value arising from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction?
      `the element of value from the transaction` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value, in dollars, arises from the accomplishment or expectation of the transaction?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fair value of my shares, leaving out the effect of the transaction` IS
    `s 262(h) the fair value of the shares` `the Court's value of the shares including the effect of the transaction` `the element of value from the transaction`

-- s 262(h). Interest from the effective date, compounded quarterly at 5% over the Federal Reserve discount rate, unless the Court for good cause determines otherwise.
-- Whole quarters only: for a part of a quarter the text gives no rule, so the answer is not covered.
@export How much interest will I be paid on the fair value (s 262(h))?
GIVEN `the fair value of my shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair value of your shares, in dollars?
      `the Court decided otherwise for good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in its discretion and for good cause shown, determined interest otherwise than as section 262(h) provides?
      `the interest the Court decided` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much interest, in dollars, did it determine?
      `the discount rate in each whole quarter` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each whole quarter from the effective date to the date of payment, what was the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge), as a fraction (for example 0.03 for 3%)? Give one number per quarter, in order.
      `the days in the part of a quarter that remains` IS A NUMBER @desc After the last whole quarter, how many days of a further part of a quarter have run? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest will I be paid on the fair value` IS
    `s 262(h) the interest on the fair value` `the fair value of my shares` courtInterest `the discount rate in each whole quarter` `the days in the part of a quarter that remains`
    WHERE
        courtInterest MEANS
            IF `the Court decided otherwise for good cause`
            THEN JUST `the interest the Court decided`
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 262(h). After the entity pays cash before judgment, interest accrues only on the difference between the payment and the fair value, plus accrued interest not paid.
@export On what sum does interest accrue after the entity pays me cash before judgment (s 262(h))?
GIVEN `the fair value of my shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair value of your shares as the Court determines it, in dollars?
      `the cash the entity paid me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much cash, in dollars, did the surviving entity pay you before judgment?
      `the interest accrued by then` IS A NUMBER @desc How much interest, in dollars, had accrued by then?
      `that interest was paid with the cash` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that accrued interest paid with the cash?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `On what sum does interest accrue after the entity pays me cash before judgment` IS
    `s 262(h) the sum on which interest accrues after a payment in cash` `the fair value of my shares` `the cash the entity paid me` `the interest accrued by then` `that interest was paid with the cash`

@export May I apply for trial on the appraisal before the persons entitled are finally determined (s 262(h))?
GIVEN `I am the surviving entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
      `I am a person entitled to participate in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person entitled to participate in the appraisal proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for trial on the appraisal before the persons entitled are finally determined` IF
    `s 262(h) the applicant may apply for trial before the persons entitled are finally determined` `I am the surviving entity` `I am a person entitled to participate in the proceeding`

@export May I participate fully in all the proceedings (s 262(h))?
GIVEN `my name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your name appear on the list filed by the surviving entity under subsection (f)?
      `it has finally been determined that I am not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it finally been determined that you are not entitled to appraisal rights?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I participate fully in all the proceedings` IF
    `s 262(h) the person may participate fully in all proceedings` `my name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` `it has finally been determined that I am not entitled`

-- s 262(i). The Court directs the entity to pay the fair value of the shares with interest, if any. Not covered where the interest is.
@export How much will the Court direct the entity to pay me (s 262(i))?
GIVEN `the fair value of my shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fair value of your shares, in dollars?
      `the Court decided otherwise for good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in its discretion and for good cause shown, determined interest otherwise than as section 262(h) provides?
      `the interest the Court decided` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much interest, in dollars, did it determine?
      `the discount rate in each whole quarter` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each whole quarter from the effective date to the date of payment, what was the Federal Reserve discount rate (including any surcharge), as a fraction (for example 0.03 for 3%)? Give one number per quarter, in order.
      `the days in the part of a quarter that remains` IS A NUMBER @desc After the last whole quarter, how many days of a further part of a quarter have run? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will the Court direct the entity to pay me` IS
    `s 262(i) the amount the Court directs the entity to pay the person` `the fair value of my shares` interest
    WHERE
        interest MEANS
            `s 262(h) the interest on the fair value` `the fair value of my shares` courtInterest `the discount rate in each whole quarter` `the days in the part of a quarter that remains`
        courtInterest MEANS
            IF `the Court decided otherwise for good cause`
            THEN JUST `the interest the Court decided`
            ELSE NOTHING

@export Can the Court's decree be enforced against an entity formed under this law (s 262(i))?
GIVEN `where the entity was formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed` @desc Under whose law was the surviving, resulting or converted entity formed? Choose one of the options.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Court's decree be enforced against an entity formed under this law` IS
    `s 262(i) the decree may be enforced as other decrees of the Court of Chancery are enforced` `where the entity was formed`

-- s 262(j). The Court may tax the costs on the parties as it deems equitable, and may charge a participating listed person's expenses pro rata against the value of the shares
-- entitled to appraisal that were not dismissed under (k).
@export May the costs of the proceeding be taxed upon me (s 262(j))?
GIVEN `I am a party to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the appraisal proceeding?
      `the Court deems it equitable to tax costs upon me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court deem it equitable in the circumstances to tax costs upon you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the costs of the proceeding be taxed upon me` IF
    `s 262(j) the costs of the proceeding may be taxed upon the person` `I am a party to the proceeding` `the Court deems it equitable to tax costs upon me`

@export May I apply for an order that my expenses be charged against the appraised shares (s 262(j))?
GIVEN `my name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your name appear on the list filed by the surviving entity under subsection (f)?
      `I participated in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in the proceeding?
      `I incurred expenses in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incur expenses in connection with the proceeding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for an order that my expenses be charged against the appraised shares` IF
    `s 262(j) the person may apply for an order that expenses be charged against the shares` `my name appears on the list filed under subsection (f)` `I participated in the proceeding` `I incurred expenses in it`

@export How much of the expenses ordered will be charged against my shares (s 262(j))?
GIVEN `the expenses the Court ordered` IS A NUMBER @desc How much in expenses, in dollars, did the Court order to be charged?
      `the value of my shares` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in dollars, of your shares entitled to appraisal?
      `the value of all the shares charged` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value, in dollars, of all the shares entitled to appraisal not dismissed under subsection (k) or subject to an award under a reservation of jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the expenses ordered will be charged against my shares` IS
    `s 262(j) the person's pro rata share of the expenses charged against the shares` `the expenses the Court ordered` `the value of my shares` `the value of all the shares charged`

-- s 262(k). After demanding, from the effective date I cannot vote the shares or receive dividends on them (other than those payable to holders of record before the effective date).
@export Am I barred from voting my shares now that I have demanded appraisal (s 262(k))?
GIVEN `I demanded appraisal for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you demanded appraisal rights for the shares?
      `my right to appraisal has since ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your right to appraisal of the shares since ceased (by withdrawal or because no petition was filed)?
      `the date of the vote` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the vote you want to cast?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from voting my shares now that I have demanded appraisal` IS
    `s 262(k) the person is barred from voting the shares` `I demanded appraisal for the shares` `my right to appraisal has since ended` `the date of the vote` `the effective date`

@export Am I barred from receiving this dividend now that I have demanded appraisal (s 262(k))?
GIVEN `I demanded appraisal for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you demanded appraisal rights for the shares?
      `my right to appraisal has since ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your right to appraisal of the shares since ceased (by withdrawal or because no petition was filed)?
      `the date the dividend is paid` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the dividend or distribution paid?
      `the record date of the dividend` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date of the dividend or distribution?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from receiving this dividend now that I have demanded appraisal` IS
    `s 262(k) the person is barred from receiving the dividend or distribution on the shares` `I demanded appraisal for the shares` `my right to appraisal has since ended` `the date the dividend is paid` `the record date of the dividend` `the effective date`

@export Does my right to appraisal of the shares end when I withdraw my demand (s 262(k))?
GIVEN `I delivered a written withdrawal to the surviving entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deliver a written withdrawal of your demand to the surviving, resulting or converted entity?
      `the date I delivered it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deliver it?
      `the corporation approved the withdrawal in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation approve the withdrawal in writing?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my right to appraisal of the shares end when I withdraw my demand` IF
    `s 262(k) the right of the person to an appraisal of the shares subject to the withdrawal ceases` `I delivered a written withdrawal to the surviving entity` `the date I delivered it` `the corporation approved the withdrawal in writing` `the effective date`

@export Is the Court's approval needed to dismiss the proceeding as to me (s 262(k))?
GIVEN `I commenced the proceeding or joined it as a named party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you commenced the appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Court's approval needed to dismiss the proceeding as to me` IF
    `s 262(k) the proceeding cannot be dismissed as to the person without the approval of the Court` `I commenced the proceeding or joined it as a named party`

@export Has the right to appraisal of all shares ended because no petition was filed in time (s 262(k))?
GIVEN `a petition has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any petition for appraisal been filed?
      `the date the first petition was filed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date was the first petition filed?
      `the effective date` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the transaction become effective?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc What is the date today (or the date you are asking about)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the right to appraisal of all shares ended because no petition was filed in time` IF
    `s 262(k) the right to appraisal with respect to all shares has ceased for want of a petition` firstPetition `the effective date` `the date I am asking about`
    WHERE
        firstPetition MEANS
            IF `a petition has been filed`
            THEN JUST `the date the first petition was filed`
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 262(l). The shares or interests that would have been issued to me but for my demand are authorized but not outstanding, until I am no longer entitled to appraisal.
@export Do the shares I would have received have the status of authorized but not outstanding (s 262(l))?
GIVEN `an appraisal demand was made in accordance with section 262` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an appraisal demand made in accordance with section 262 for the shares they would have been issued for?
      `the person who demanded is still entitled to appraisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who demanded appraisal still entitled to appraisal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the shares I would have received have the status of authorized but not outstanding` IF
    `s 262(l) the shares or equity interests have the status of authorized but not outstanding` `an appraisal demand was made in accordance with section 262` `the person who demanded is still entitled to appraisal`
